From 8dfe47b14934778f02ff16126eb7ba42560ad5a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:05:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bootwait: redesigned waiter screen (triangle X emblem in text
 VRAM, frame, colours, aligned fields)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- Emblem: our own geometric mark, four triangles meeting at the centre to
  form an X, plus a heavy italic "X68000 Z" with a drop shadow, 464x80 px,
  drawn straight into text VRAM planes 2-3 (planes 0-1 stay IOCS text).
  Generated by driver/mkbootwait.py (PIL, Arial Black sheared) into
  driver/bootwait_gen.S together with all strings and positions; the
  generated file is committed so the build needs no PIL.
- Text palette 1-3 (teal / amber / white) and 4/8/12 (emblem red, shadow,
  orange); the ROM palette is saved at start and restored, planes 2-3
  cleared, colour 3, screen cleared and the cursor turned back on before
  the real IPL or the setting UI runs.
- Box-drawing frame, centred subtitle and title, aligned Wi-Fi / SMB /
  HDS / 経過 fields with ● (connected, teal) / ○ (waiting, amber) /
  × (cannot open), IP and next-retry text, a ◆ travelling along a ━ line
  between [Pico W] and [X68000 Z], a reverse-video key bar at the bottom,
  cursor off. Every field is redrawn at an absolute position and padded
  to a fixed width; CRTC R21/R23 cleared before each print.
- Stage 2 grows to 12 KB: BW_STAGE2 is now 32 sectors (ID 6 LBA
  0x80-0x9f), loaded to $2800 by stage 1 (must stay below settingui at
  $67c0, asserted). Variables moved to $7000.
- waiter_test.py models the IOCS text screen (ESC[2J / ESC[y;xH /
  Shift_JIS widths / B_COLOR), text VRAM and the palette: checks the
  frame, labels and columns, field values over time, the travelling
  packet, the reverse bar, the emblem bytes in planes 2-3, palette and
  cursor while waiting, and full restore before the IPL and the setting
  UI. It renders waiter_preview.png (text + emblem with the palette).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
